==Overview==
<tabber>
|-|Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* High combo potential.
* All moves can be used in a combo for excellent damage output. The Z and C moves are good for running away when the players health is low.
* Very good knockback.
* Good damage.
* Great for [[Raids]] since the player can use the Z move to stun the raid boss so others can also hit it.
* Good [[Fighting Styles|fighting style]] for traveling.
* Does not cost any [[Fragments]] to buy, unlike the V2 [[Fighting Styles|fighting styles]].
* Both the [Z] and [C] moves combo into each other, and the user can follow this up with [[Flash Step]] and [X].
* Decent alternative to [[Godhuman]].

|'''[Z] Beast Owl Pounce'''
* Decent for mobility.
* Long stun.
* Brief cooldown.
* Decent for draining opponent's [[Instinct]] because of tick damage if they try to Instinct-trick.
* Good for traveling long distances.

|'''[X] Thunder Clap'''
* [[Instinct Break|Breaks Instinct]] if hit in the middle.
* Big AOE.

|'''[C] Conqueror Gun'''
* Decent for mobility.
* Good damage.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Underwhelming compared to its upgraded version, [[Godhuman]]
* Very time-consuming to unlock, just like its successor, Godhuman (Costs {{Money|3,000,000}}, and players need to grind four [[fighting styles]] to 300 mastery). The player also needs to be in [[Second Sea]] or above.
* Slow [M1] attacks
* It is more efficient to just get [[Water Kung Fu]], [[Dark Step]], or [[Electric]] to 400 mastery and then getting [[Sharkman Karate]], [[Death Step]] or [[Electric Claw]] with it, which are better than [[Superhuman]] in terms of grinding.
* Horrible for grinding, as [Z] and [C] are single target, and [X] has a ton of knockback.
* Moves are not recommended while using [[Buddha]] or hunting [[Sea Events]].
* All moves can be dodged easily if used individually rather than as a consecutive combo.

|'''[Z] Beast Owl Pounce'''
* Lower damage if hit from afar.
* Can be dodged with [[Instinct]] while still using the attack.
* Locks the user in place for a significant amount of time without I-frames, so the user can get easily targeted. This also leads to the move being risky for grinding.
* Hard to hit because the move itself is generally slow travel.

|'''[X] Thunder Clap'''
* Can be dodged with [[Instinct]] if the user doesn't directly hit the target.
* Hard to land.
* Leaves the user very vulnerable to counterattacks.
* Small range.
* Does not affect players above or below the user.
* Doesn't work on [[Sea Beast]]s.

|'''[C] Conqueror Gun'''
* Can be dodged with [[Instinct]].
* Only works on [[Sea Beast]]s when close enough, leaving the user vulnerable.
}}

|-|Notes=
{{Overview|Notes
|
* Superhuman is not very good for farming levels due to its high knockback, but its PvP potential makes up for it.
** Superhuman can be effectively used for farming if using [[Buddha]] due to the [Z] move increasing range.
* Superhuman requires a lot of skill and aim to use effectively.
* Superhuman's M1 (tap) leaves a white trail for a split second, just like how Instinct V2 leaves a trail when enabled.
* When the player hits a target, '''[Z] Beast Owl Pounce''' deals 50% the damage of the total damage and the collision will also deal 50% of '''[Z] Beast Owl Pounce'''.
* When using '''[Z] Beast Owl Pounce''' on a target that has low [[health]], the user simply travels through and kill the target without punching the target.
}}
